  <div id="sutta">
  
    <h4 id="thig3.4" class="h1">Thig 3:4  Dantikā &amp; the Elephant</h4>
          <div class="verse">
            <p>Coming out from my day’s abiding</p>
            <p>on Vulture Peak Mountain,</p>
            <p>I saw on the bank of the river</p>
            <p class="v2">an elephant</p>
            <p>emerged from its plunge.</p>
            <div class="verse-add">
              <p>A man holding a hook requested:</p>
              <p class="v4">“Give me your foot.”</p>
              <p>The elephant</p>
              <p class="v1">extended its foot.</p>
              <p>The man</p>
              <p class="v1">got up on the elephant.</p>
            </div><!--end verse-add-->
            <div class="verse-add">
              <p>Seeing what was untrained now tamed</p>
              <p>brought under human control,</p>
              <p>with that I centered my mind—</p>
              <p class="v1">why I’d gone to the woods</p>
              <p class="v4">in the first place.</p>
            </div><!--end verse-add-->
          </div><!--end verse-->
      </div><!--end:sutta-->
    </div><!--end:content-->
    
